# Item: WC enum-case return type rescue in tryTypeFirstExtensionEntity
# Track: P (Printer parity)
# Started: 2026-04-28T19:20Z
# Committed: d17c785

## Root Cause

`tryTypeFirstExtensionEntity` parsed `yA2EmFWC` correctly for the
params slot (Type(BuiltinTypeName("...Placeholder.Type"))), but built
the function text with `verboseRetStr(true)` BEFORE the outer
`tryEntitySuffix` got a chance to handle the `WC` suffix. Since
`retNode = nil` (void, from the leading `y`), `verboseRetStr` emitted
`" -> ()"`, producing:

```
enum case for (extension in Foundation):Swift.String.LocalizationValue.Placeholder.int(...Placeholder.Type) -> ()
```

The WC rescue already existed in `tryFunctionEntity` (line 10135) but
`tryTypeFirstExtensionEntity` is a separate code path with its own
result/params parser — it never called tryFunctionEntity.

## Fix

Added a WC rescue block in `tryTypeFirstExtensionEntity` between the
`F`-consuming increment and the `wrap.Text` construction (lines
6611-6621 after fix):

When all of the following hold:
- `retNode == nil` (void result from leading `y`)
- exactly one param with `KindType → KindBuiltinTypeName` and `.Type` suffix
- `WC` follows in input

→ set `retNode` to `Type(BuiltinTypeName(base))` where
`base = strings.TrimSuffix(paramTypes[0].Children[0].Text, ".Type")`.

This causes `verboseRetStr(true)` to emit
`" -> (extension in Foundation):Swift.String.LocalizationValue.Placeholder"`,
which after outer `tryEntitySuffix("WC")` prepends "enum case for "
yields the correct full string.

## Symbols Fixed

All 8 `LocalizationValue.Placeholder.int(...)` enum case symbols:
- `$sSS10FoundationE17LocalizationValueV11PlaceholderO3intyA2EmFWC`
  GOT: `...Placeholder.int(...Type) -> ()`
  WANT: `...Placeholder.int(...Type) -> ...Placeholder`
- 7 additional variants with the same pattern.

